{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And you shall observe to do as YHWH your Elohim has commanded you</b> — this is a warning concerning the Ten Commandments that HaShem commanded them from His own mouth, and afterwards He warns concerning the rest of the commandments, which they were to hear from Moses and perform. Therefore it says (Deuteronomy 6:1), <b>Now this is the commandment, the statutes and the judgments, which YHWH your Elohim commanded to teach you</b>, for HaShem acknowledged your words and commanded me to teach you the rest of the entire Torah, <b>that you may live</b> — that your days may be fulfilled, and <b>that it may be well with you</b> with all the goodness that He promised you in the portion of <i>If in My statutes</i> and elsewhere, and <b>that your days may be prolonged upon the land</b>, that you may inherit it for your children forever."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:54.993404194Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}